  "body": "@slightlyoff pointed out that we might be able to use `Object.observe` instead of events to track changes to various bits of Bluetooth metadata. For example, if we define `BluetoothDevice.prototype.services` as the cached array of discovered `BluetoothGattServices`, we could observe it for changes instead of needing to define the [serviceadded, etc. events](https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#service-change-events). We'd need to be clear that this is a cache like `BluetoothGattCharacteristic.value` (#37), rather than an up-front-discovered list of all the services.\n\nSimilarly, we could define a `navigator.bluetooth.connectedDevices` array to handle devices getting disconnected and reconnected (#31). That also handles the problem of a re-opened web page finding the devices it already has access to.\n",
